text:
Race condition. Multiple requests read same value before any write commit.

## Fix options

**1. Atomic update (best)**
```sql
UPDATE counters
SET value = value + 1
WHERE id = $1
RETURNING value;
```
DB handle increment atomically. No read-then-write gap.

**2. Row-level lock**
```sql
BEGIN;
SELECT value FROM counters WHERE id = $1 FOR UPDATE;
-- now safe to read, others block here
UPDATE counters SET value = value + 1 WHERE id = $1 RETURNING value;
COMMIT;
```
Use when need value before update for other logic.

**3. Advisory lock** — overkill here, skip.

## Node code (option 1)

```js
app.post('/increment/:id', async (req, res) => {
  const { rows } = await pool.query(
    'UPDATE counters SET value = value + 1 WHERE id = $1 RETURNING value',
    [req.params.id]
  );
  if (!rows.length) return res.status(404).json({ error: 'Not found' });
  res.json({ value: rows[0].value });
});
```

## Why current code breaks

```js
// BROKEN
const { rows } = await pool.query('SELECT value FROM counters WHERE id = $1', [id]);
const newVal = rows[0].value + 1;          // req A and B both read 5
await pool.query('UPDATE counters SET value = $1 WHERE id = $2', [newVal, id]);
// both write 6. one increment lost.
```

**Use option 1.** Single round-trip, no locks, scales well.
